        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Chagres National Park and an Emberá village"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "d464b7eae1c09cabaebb73409b1e955553c89b1c8327991e261f40ad2a619d38",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-63081f33d4c840e99362579a12d8b39a",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "The excursion runs from 08:00 to 16:00. You’ll leave early for Chagres National Park. Travel along the river and through the jungle to a waterfall, where you’ll have time to swim.\n\nIndigenous guides will then take you by raft to the village of Tusipono. Your hosts welcome you with music played on traditional instruments, serve an Indigenous lunch and perform traditional dances.\n\nThe Emberá are known for their woodcarving and other crafts. In the village, you can buy cocobolo woodwork, small sculptures carved from nuts or bone, and baskets woven from chunga palm leaves. Return to your hotel after the visit."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_label:b46c908b07252155",
      "field": "itinerary.label",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1aedcc37eb28bb5b2a01a00af5b58e1d1984b8649dd2d761c0c2b93680491e83",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-63081f33d4c840e99362579a12d8b39a",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Chagres National Park"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:2f2a89429b893ecf",
